/-!
# `Work.CharCore.isChar_regularChar`

The character of the regular representation `Work.CharCore.regularChar G` (value `|G|` at `1`
and `0` elsewhere) is an honest character: it lies in the additive monoid generated by the
irreducible characters.

Indeed, pairing it with an irreducible character `χ` localises the defining sum at the
identity,

  `⟨regularChar G, χ⟩ = |G|⁻¹ ∑_x (if x = 1 then |G| else 0) * conj (χ x) = conj (χ 1)`,

and `χ 1 = irrDeg χ : ℂ` is a natural number, hence fixed by complex conjugation
(`Work.CharCore.cfInner_regularChar`).  Thus every inner product `⟨regularChar G, χ⟩` with
`χ ∈ Irr G` is a natural number, and the character criterion `Work.CharCore.isChar_iff`
exhibits `regularChar G` as the non-negative integral combination `∑_χ (irrDeg χ : ℂ) • χ`
of the irreducible characters (equivalently, as the decomposition of the regular
representation).
-/

noncomputable section

open Classical

namespace Work.CharCore

/-- **The regular character is an honest character**: its inner products with all
irreducible characters are the natural numbers `irrDeg χ`. -/
theorem isChar_regularChar {G : Type*} [Group G] [Fintype G] : IsChar (regularChar G) :=
  (isChar_iff (isClassFun_regularChar G)).mpr
    (fun χ hχ => ⟨irrDeg χ, cfInner_regularChar hχ⟩)

end Work.CharCore
